WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
- I have this song, "Piece by Piece,"

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.250
and I'm the writer.
- Yes.

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.220
And, (laughs)

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:04.960
and it was all about like, for me,

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.930
it was like I'd never really experienced

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.040
the loss of my father.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.060
Like how it...

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.410
It never impacted me
until I became a parent.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.998
'Cause then I knew what a parent should be

00:00:12.998 --> 00:00:14.250
and what it felt like.
- Amen.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.600
And I was like, oh, I
didn't really know the loss.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.640
I didn't know the impact.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.422
And so I wrote this song and, you know,

00:00:21.422 --> 00:00:23.800
it ended up being like,

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.070
I wrote the song for like my daughter

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.070
and my husband at the time.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.930
And little did I know it was
only a piece of this puzzle,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:31.810
this full puzzle,

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.560
'cause like now,
- It's a page.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.670
I have the, it's yeah,

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.250
and I have this whole full
puzzle sitting in front of me.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.630
Well, what I think is, you never know.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.540
And literally there's a
lyric on my new album,

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.287
in a song called
(indistinct), and it's like,

00:00:44.287 --> 00:00:47.790
"By the way, piece by piece,
I found out my hero is me."

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.340
And it's
- Oh, what a beautiful thing.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.380
Yeah!

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.320
Well, 'cause it's like, and
not like in a negative sense,

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.520
in like a way of like,

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.210
it's almost too much to put on someone

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.100
to do that for you.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.280
You know, you have to do that,

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:58.800
like kind of yourself, piece by piece.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.420
You have to get there yourself.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.206
But it's so funny, 'cause
that's the, I'm the writer.

00:01:03.206 --> 00:01:04.039
- Right!

00:01:04.039 --> 00:01:05.930
- And I was like, I was a little off.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.900
I was like, but I got there.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.670
I was like, it's okay. (laughs)

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:10.950
- But that's, you know,

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.167
like Eric Clapton gets
the credit for this quote.

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.790
"My greatest work is my greatest work,

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:17.620
I just held the pen."

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:18.690
And so I think it's...

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:21.026
I think it's God kind
of doing their thing,

00:01:21.026 --> 00:01:21.859
they're doing this thing
- You're the vessel.

00:01:21.859 --> 00:01:22.692
the way they do.

00:01:22.692 --> 00:01:25.120
And even you as a writer,
there's gonna be something,

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.310
if the song is timeless,

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.450
will come back to you and present itself,

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.930
and you go, I never knew it that way.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:33.753
- [Kelly] Yeah, I agree, I agree.

